WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.050
On December 25, 1991, the Soviet
flag came down over the Kremlin.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.730
The Soviet Union became
15 separate states.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.810
Then, on July 9, 2011, South Sudan
became independent from Sudan.

4
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.490
Belgium took another path.

5
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:22.870
It became a federal state, with Flemish,
Brussels-Capital and Walloon regions.

6
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.470
Why do some states break apart,
while others hold together?

7
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.670
In this mission, you'll uncover what
pulls power away from a country's capital.

8
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.150
Then you'll see how radio, the internet
and social media help movements spread

9
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.710
their ideas.

10
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.850
Your mission: explain why
some countries split apart,

11
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.730
while others hand power to their regions.
